    "identifier": "storm-herald-typhoon-storm-terror",
    "description": "<p>Starting at 14th Level, your Crash, Herald state rages upending stone and other unattended objects. When you would act as a Herald, by spending 2 Focus as part of entering the enhanced state, you instead become a Typhoon. While a Typhoon you gain the benefits of being a Herald, you gain 1 Pressure at the end of each of your turns and you may use the base effects of Gale Burst, Sharpening or Dragwind once per turn, at no Pressure cost.</p>\n<p>But while a Typhoon, hostile creatures gain a +2 bonus to their attack rolls and +1 critical threat range when attacking you.</p>",
